1
00:00:00,113 --> 00:00:03,112
How far is every vertex from s?

2
00:00:03,112 --> 00:00:04,425
And can some vertex

3
00:00:04,425 --> 00:00:05,375
never be reached?

4
00:00:05,954 --> 00:00:08,329
Level zero is just s,

5
00:00:08,329 --> 00:00:09,579
at distance zero.

6
00:00:10,187 --> 00:00:12,488
Level one is every unvisited

7
00:00:12,488 --> 00:00:14,300
neighbour of level zero,

8
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,300
at distance one.

9
00:00:15,887 --> 00:00:17,788
Level two grows only

10
00:00:17,788 --> 00:00:18,887
from level one.

11
00:00:18,887 --> 00:00:21,775
Edges back to s are rejected; b,

12
00:00:21,775 --> 00:00:23,487
d and e are new.

13
00:00:24,087 --> 00:00:26,862
Level three: only f is new,

14
00:00:26,862 --> 00:00:28,025
found from d.

15
00:00:28,025 --> 00:00:30,950
Every other edge, even e to f,

16
00:00:30,950 --> 00:00:31,813
is rejected.

17
00:00:32,387 --> 00:00:34,887
Level four is empty, so we stop.

18
00:00:34,887 --> 00:00:36,862
g was never reached:

19
00:00:36,862 --> 00:00:38,762
its distance is infinity.

20
00:00:39,367 --> 00:00:41,942
Slide each vertex into its level.

21
00:00:41,942 --> 00:00:43,454
No edge skips a level;

22
00:00:43,804 --> 00:00:45,892
only d to e stays inside one.

23
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:47,675
So reaching f takes

24
00:00:47,675 --> 00:00:49,438
at least three edges,

25
00:00:49,438 --> 00:00:50,150
and the green tree

26
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:52,350
path uses exactly three.

27
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:55,179
The cost: eight edges,

28
00:00:55,179 --> 00:00:56,729
each checked from both ends,

29
00:00:56,729 --> 00:00:58,380
so sixteen checks.

30
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:00,479
Linear time, order V plus E.

31
00:01:01,067 --> 00:01:02,817
Each level is the unvisited

32
00:01:02,817 --> 00:01:04,429
neighbours of the level before,

33
00:01:04,829 --> 00:01:06,217
and a vertex's level

34
00:01:06,217 --> 00:01:07,305
is its distance.
